            <ArticleTitle>Creatine kinase elevation after scleral buckling.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>45-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A two- to three-fold elevation in serum creatine kinase levels were found in patients postoperatively after scleral buckling procedures. Further fractionation revealed the myocardial band (CK-MB) to be absent; with skeletal muscle (CK-MM) contributing to the enzyme elevation. Isoenzymes are recommended in postoperative patients when myocardial infarction is considered.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
